// The HRESULTs the SASec methods return ([MS-TSCH] 3.2.5.3, [MS-ERREF] 2.1) are not
// declared here. The whole of [MS-ERREF] 2.1.1 lives in
// github.com/TheManticoreProject/Manticore/windows/errors/hresult as the HRESULT type,
// and the six values repeated here covered six of that 2928-value table while drifting
// from it. Convert a returned status with hresult.HRESULT(status) and test
// hresult.HRESULT.IsSuccess, which is the severity bit [MS-TSCH] 3.2.5.3 describes and
// not a comparison against zero, since for an HRESULT success is a range.
//
// Three of the six were FACILITY_WIN32 wrappings, 0x80070002, 0x8007000D and 0x8007052E,
// and those need no declaration at all: [MS-ERREF] 2.1.2 makes such a name a computation
// over the Win32 code the low half carries, which the shared table performs, so they
// render as HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND) and its siblings rather than as the
// bare Win32 names the removed switch returned — the value is an HRESULT, not the code it
// wraps. Build one with hresult.FromWin32(win32.ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND) and unwrap it with
// hresult.HRESULT.ToWin32.

